# Per-subdirectory, not a blanket `data/` rule - data/warehouse.db and
# data/topics/ are committed on purpose (see the exception block below).
# `data/` as a single directory-level pattern would make a later
# `!data/warehouse.db` negation a no-op: git never descends into an
# already-ignored directory to check file-level exceptions.
data/raw/
data/ingested/
data/validated/
data/scored/
data/embedded/

models/*.joblib
models/*.pkl
models/hf_cache/
*.db
__pycache__/
.venv/
evaluation/*.csv

# Exception: the two artifacts config/pipeline.yaml currently pins, committed
# deliberately so a fresh clone (e.g. a free hosting deploy) can run
# pipeline.score / pipeline.topics without retraining - these load a pinned
# sha and never retrain by design, so without this exception a fresh clone
# would only have models/registry.json pointing at files that don't exist.
# Bump this exception by hand whenever the pin in config/pipeline.yaml
# changes (see docs/decisions.md) - it is never updated automatically.
!models/tfidf_logreg_baseline-f732ce395686.joblib
!models/bertopic-d62f4dfa6044.pkl

# Exception: data/warehouse.db + data/topics/ - committed 2026-10-18 after
# the live rebuild-on-deploy approach (dashboard/bootstrap.py) proved
# unreliable on Streamlit Community Cloud's free tier (CPU throttling
# produced a fully blank page once, then a silently incomplete build a
# second time, neither with any visible error - see docs/decisions.md).
# dashboard/app.py reads only these two paths, not the rest of data/, so
# this is the minimum needed for the dashboard to show real, verified
# output (66 alerts, 54/12 split) instantly with zero compute on deploy.
# bootstrap.py is left in place as a harmless fallback - its fast path
# (data already present) is a no-op once these files exist.
!data/warehouse.db
!data/topics/
